@startuml
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "User (Browser)" as User
participant "Frontend" as FE
box "Infrastructure" #f9f9f9
    participant "Nginx" as Nginx
    participant "API Gateway\n(Auth Proxy)" as GW
    database "Redis\n(Sessions)" as Redis
end box
participant "Collab Service\n(Socket.IO + REST)" as Collab

== Phase 1: Ticket Acquisition ==

User -> FE: Wants to join session
FE -> Nginx: POST /api/collab/join\n{sessionId}\nAuth: [Firebase Token]
Nginx -> GW: Forward (strip /api)
activate GW
GW -> GW: Validate Firebase Token\n(extract uid, inject X-User-Id)
GW -> Collab: POST /collab/join\n(X-User-Id: uid, body: {sessionId})
deactivate GW
activate Collab
Collab -> Redis: GET session:{id}:meta
Redis --> Collab: {user1_id, user2_id, ...}
Collab -> Collab: Check uid in [user1_id, user2_id]
Collab -> Redis: SET ticket:{UUID}\n{uid, sessionId} EX 60
Collab --> GW: 200 OK { ticket: "UUID" }
deactivate Collab
GW --> FE: 200 OK { ticket: "UUID" }

note over FE
  Frontend acquires **two tickets** — one for
  /editor and one for /chat (separate namespaces).
end note

== Phase 2: WebSocket Connection (per namespace) ==

FE -> Nginx: WS Upgrade Request\n/socket.io/?ticket=UUID
activate Nginx
Nginx -> Collab: Proxy Upgrade\n(plain passthrough, no auth_request)
activate Collab

Collab -> Collab: Socket.IO middleware:\nextract ticket from query

Collab -> Redis: GETDEL ticket:{UUID}
Redis --> Collab: {uid, sessionId} or null

alt Ticket Valid
    Collab -> Collab: Attach userId & sessionId\nto socket object
    Collab --> FE: HTTP 101 Switching Protocols
    FE <-> Collab: Authenticated WebSocket
else Ticket Invalid/Expired/Missing
    Collab --> FE: Connection rejected\n(Socket.IO error event)
end

deactivate Collab
deactivate Nginx

== Phase 3: Editor Namespace — Yjs Sync ==

FE -> Collab: Connected to /editor
activate Collab
Collab -> Collab: getOrCreateSession(sessionId)
Collab -> Redis: LRANGE session:{id}:ydoc 0 -1
Redis --> Collab: [base64 updates...]
Collab -> Collab: Replay updates into Y.Doc
Collab -> FE: emit 'yjs-sync' (full state)
Collab -> FE: emit 'user-joined' for each\nexisting connected user
Collab --> Collab: Broadcast 'user-joined'\nto partner in room
deactivate Collab

== Phase 4: Chat Namespace — History Load ==

FE -> Collab: Connected to /chat
activate Collab
Collab -> Redis: LRANGE session:{id}:chat -50 -1
Redis --> Collab: [last 50 messages]
Collab -> FE: emit 'chat-history' (messages[])
deactivate Collab

note over Collab, Redis
  Design notes:
  - Ticket issuance: POST /collab/join handled by collab-service
    (proxied through API Gateway for auth injection).
  - Ticket validation happens in collab service
    middleware, not via nginx auth_request
    (auth_request interferes with WebSocket upgrades).
  - Each namespace (/editor, /chat) requires
    its own one-time ticket for connection.
  - Yjs updates are persisted as base64 in a Redis
    list and replayed on session load.
end note

@enduml
